  "evidence": "Original Delray listing documents ALT1-C/BL, 43mm steel case, automatic chronograph/date and used calf strap; specimen manufacture year is unstated. Eleven gallery files inspected (ten scenes plus smaller front rendition). Actual blue dial has pale subdials at three/nine, date at six, CHRONOMETER and LONDON; actual display back has AUTOMATIC / BREMONT / CHRONOMETER / 10 ATM inscriptions. Visible movement has a Bremont signed decorated rotor, blue screws and visible bridge finishing; no legible calibre stamp and no base-calibre equivalence established. Manufacturer retired ALT1-C Blue page describes a 2018 redesign and BE-50AE specification, but those dates/specifications do not prove this particular specimen date, physical calibre, pressure rating or current accuracy. Generic ALT1-C is explicitly representative of this blue steel/leather execution, not cream ALT1-C-CR, gold, black, polished-white or other suffixes. Signed pin buckle and worn blue leather are fitted specimen hardware; factory originality is not established. No paperwork photograph promoted.",
